LCHAT-42 Merge main - embedding models, RAG eval and the benchmark charts

Mostly additive on both sides: main's embedding models, re-embedding, embedding
benchmark and RAG evaluation alongside this branch's benchmark charts and turn
timing. Query keys, service functions, route table and stylesheets keep both.

Three resolutions that were not just "keep both":

localFiles.ts takes main's version - folder walking, a skipped[] list and the
drop caps are all better than what was here - EXCEPT that main's pickInBrowser
sets input.accept, which is the bug this branch removed. macOS resolves each
extension in accept to a Uniform Type Identifier and .md has none registered, so
the dialog lists markdown files and then refuses to let you select them. The
folder picker keeps its accept: there you choose a directory, not a file, and
isAcceptedFile filters the walk afterwards.

ChatPage's ingestNote is deleted in favour of main's notification stack. Both
reported the same rejections, so both would have fired; main's is better placed,
raised by the mutation itself so it still reports when you have navigated away.
main's addDocuments also handles skipped files and passes alsoGeneral from the
chat's scope, neither of which this branch's version did.

ChatPage's own rejection test moves onto the notification stack rather than
being deleted: a drop onto the transcript is a different entry point from the
Add files button GeneralDocumentsPage covers, and it is the one reached for
mid-conversation.

Settings.module.css needed two closing braces put back by hand. .chartControls
and .evalSummaryRow happen to end with the same two declarations, as do
.chartEmpty and .evalStat's neighbours, so git treated the shared trailer as one
line and closed only whichever rule came last.

